WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.437
When we group by product Spark must bring rows with
the same product together If

00:00:06.463 --> 00:00:12.269
those rows are spread across partitions the engine
needs a shuffle This

00:00:12.295 --> 00:00:17.876
is why aggregation is not just a mathematical step
In distributed execution

00:00:18.113 --> 00:00:20.113
it also has a data-movement cost
